<title>FRANCE: Alcatel confirms contacts with GEC.</title>
<headline>Alcatel confirms contacts with GEC.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Alcatel Alsthom on Friday confirmed that it had had contacts with Britain's General Electric Company Plc (GEC) about the privatisation of Thomson-CSF.</p>
<p>Alcatel chairman Serge Tchuruk has made no secret of his intention to conclude European ventures in the event that Alcatel and Dassault Industrie were selected as buyer of the state's 58-percent stake in Thonson-CSF.</p>
<p>On March 18, he said he aimed to conclude deals with both Germany's Daimler-Benz Aerospace and GEC, but he did not want to make early commitments.  </p>
<p>&quot;We confirm that we have had contacts with GEC,&quot; an Alcatel spokesman said on Friday.</p>
</text>
